Existing-test changes for spec 3f70cc03aeae9c1a (round 4). Rule: expectations only, intent preserved, nothing weakened.
Reasons by file (R id: reason):
- R14 (versions.analysis "6"): test_search_mimicry_metrics.py, test_search_mimicry_schema_and_structure.py (test renamed ..._is_6_...), test_structure_integration.py, legacy_metric_transition_support.py (old "3" payload is converted to the current version), standalone_candidate_policy_support.py (same conversion).
- R11 (evidence_spread fires on >= 2 directories outside the target's directory, metrics gain directory_count): test_signal_defects.py V7 (files moved into directories a/, b/, c/ so the original file-count cases still hold; metrics gain directory_count), test_bottlenecks_v3.py (evidence_subject and three_kind_subject use b/b.py and c/c.py; single-file cases keep a root target and root evidence so directory_count is 0), test_file_analysis_core.py test_V06_two_files_spread (p/a.py and q/d.py; directory_count 2 asserted additionally), test_ambiguous_candidates.py (VO4 cases: source, user and target files in separate directories; directory_count 2 asserted additionally), standalone_candidate_policy_support._spread (independent oracle now follows R11: directories other than the target's, directory_count in metrics).
- R11r (card shows directory_count): report_redesign_support.py, file_analysis_browser_support.py, unified_support.py add directory_count to synthetic evidence_spread metrics; test_report_modal.py gives file_count 6 / directory_count 5 and now asserts the card shows 5 and not 6 (stronger than before).
Not changed here (needs the main role): tests/test_nestjs_quality.py O11 compares against tests/ambiguous_candidates_evidence/standalone-originals.json.gz, whose Kotlin/android raw nodes differ after R13 (constructor field span/cost/signature); the archive must be regenerated as in round 3.
